# Wave W17-AC (Route 230): palm sand — palm-shore sand, warm flecks: a warm pale sand under the harbour run’s shallows, carrying gold flecks where the sun reaches the bottom off Palmside’s shore (design: the west coast water — north at the point, Clashfield harbour; the circuit closes). Route 230’s own sand — split from its twin Route 229’s loop sand by warmth entire (palm-shore warm vs offshore cool) and from Route 219’s bright sand by shore: harbour-run gold here, beach-road gold there, told apart by density — this sand is scattered off a point, that one lies thick off a beach.
